Z||000002||mrfiero||09-17-2001||12:21 PM||||First you need to figure out why you think your rotors are bad.  What makes you think that they are (i.e. symptoms)?<P>Unless they are out of spec, as far as thickness goes, they can be resurfaced (turned) and will be good as new.  The most common problem with rotors is warpage......by resurfacing them you eliminate the warpage, but again, the minimum thickness plays an important role.<P>If they are gouged up pretty bad then you likely have other brake issues, like sticking or frozen calipers/slide pins, etc.<P>I also have some rotors.......several good used ones and a couple of brand new ones (if you need them).<BR>||||reg||1
